{
    "background_story": "Sweetness was a majestic Italian thoroughbred named after the famous Italian poet Giosu\u00e8 Carducci. Born on a picturesque Tuscan farm, she was bred for speed and agility. As a young filly, Sweetness showed great promise, quickly becoming a favorite among the farm's trainers. Her owner, a literature enthusiast, saw a kindred spirit in the spirited mare and named her after the poet who embodied the essence of Italian culture. As Sweetness grew, she proved to be a force to be reckoned with on the track, earning numerous accolades and admiration from fans. But it was her gentle nature and affectionate personality that truly made her a beloved champion, living up to the poetic ideals of her namesake, Carducci.",
